%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 53e72f983de76b64da2c3ba9d6e008e2, type: 3}
  m_Name: GuideBookData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::GuideBookData
  pages:
  - title: How to Move
    bodyText: 'Every step counts. Each turn, you can navigate to any adjacent hex
      highlighted in Yellow. These highlights represent your valid paths across the
      battlefield.

'
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Movement
    subCategory: 
  - title: Better Movement
    bodyText: You begin your journey with 1 Move per turn. Choose your path wisely,
      but keep an eye out for powerful Perks that grant extra moves, allowing you
      to outmaneuver even the swiftest foes.
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Movement
    subCategory: 
  - title: How to Attack
    bodyText: 'There is no separate attack button. Engaging an enemy in close-quarters
      combat (by moving directly adjacent to them) triggers a Dice Roll to determine
      your damage.  '
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Combat
    subCategory: Attacking
  - title: Powering Up Your Rolls
    bodyText: 'You begin your journey with 2 dice, but as you progress, increasing
      your dice count is the key to unlocking devastating power.

'
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Combat
    subCategory: Dice
  - title: The Dice Panel
    bodyText: 'Keep a close watch on the Dice Panel: high-impact combos and Critical
      Hits  (which multiply your total damage) are highlighted in real-time. Strategize
      with unique Perks to manipulate your rolls and bend the odds in your favor!'
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Combat
    subCategory: Dice
  - title: Spikes
    bodyText: Deals damage to anyone who stepped on it.
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Combat
    subCategory: Hazards
  - title: Interruption
    bodyText: Attacking an enemy while they were ready for attacking interrupts their
      attack for one turn.
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Combat
    subCategory: Interactions
  - title: Stunning
    bodyText: Knocking an enemy into a wall stuns that enemy for one turn. If you
      knock an enemy into another enemy they both get stunned.
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Combat
    subCategory: Interactions
  - title: Choosing to Skip
    bodyText: 'At any point during your movement phase, you may choose to Skip your
      turn instead of relocating. This is a vital defensive maneuver. '
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Combat
    subCategory: Skipping
  - title: Skip Attacking
    bodyText: If you are already positioned adjacent to enemies when you Skip, you
      will immediately initiate a strike against them.
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Combat
    subCategory: Skipping
  - title: Implants With Skipping Features
    bodyText: Certain Implants are specifically engineered to provide massive bonuses
      when you choose to stand your ground and use this feature.
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Combat
    subCategory: Skipping
  - title: The Walker
    bodyText: 'Moves directly toward the player and attacks once in melee range.

      Easy
      to kite, but don''t let them corner you!'
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Enemies
    subCategory: Enemy Bestiary
  - title: The Bruiser
    bodyText: An heavy enemy that gets in mid-range. Charges a fist slam that damages
      3 tiles in a line and deals two damage. Slow but hard hitting.
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Enemies
    subCategory: Enemy Bestiary
  - title: Warlock
    bodyText: A ranged specialist that maintains maximum distance. Charges a deadly
      two-attack combo every 3rd turn that deals two damage each. Automatically teleports
      to a new location whenever it takes damage.
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Enemies
    subCategory: Enemy Bestiary
  - title: Totem
    bodyText: "Stationary structure that grants the Boss invulnerability.  \nYou
      must destroy all Totems to damage the Boss.  \nBreaking a Totem instantly clears
      all remaining minor enemies and triggers a new enemy wave.  "
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Enemies
    subCategory: Boss & Special Mechanics
  - title: The Boss
    bodyText: "Readies an arena-wide blast every 3rd turn that hits almost every
      tile that deals two damage.\nTeleports away from the player every time he is
      hit.  \nSpawns new minions each time he takes damage. \n\n"
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Enemies
    subCategory: Boss & Special Mechanics
  - title: Funding Your Run
    bodyText: "Gold is acquired by eliminating enemies. Efficient combat and specific
      Gold-boosting Perks are the best ways to ensure you can always afford the most
      powerful items in the Merchant\u2019s collection."
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Shop
    subCategory: Gold
  - title: What Are Items?
    bodyText: "Items provide a variety of persistent perks or immediate boosts to
      your combat efficiency. \n"
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Shop
    subCategory: Items
  - title: Currency and Rerolls
    bodyText: "If the current selection doesn\u2019t suit your build, you can pay
      to Reroll the inventory. Be tactical with your spending, as the cost of rerolling
      increases each time you use it."
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Shop
    subCategory: Items
  - title: Enhancement Selection
    bodyText: After successfully clearing a room, you will be granted the opportunity
      to select a new Implant. These are permanent passive upgrades that integrate
      into your system and persist for the remainder of your run.
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Implants
    subCategory: 
  - title: Rarities
    bodyText: 'Implants are categorized into five distinct tiers of rarity:


      Common
      (Grey)


      Rare (Blue)


      Epic (Purple)


      Legendary (Gold)


      ???
      (???)

'
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Implants
    subCategory: 
  - title: Synergies & Combinations
    bodyText: The key to a successful run lies in your ability to build Synergies.
      Experiment with different Implant combinations to unlock devastating technical
      advantages and create a build that can withstand any threat. Keep playing and
      you may find something interesting like -???-.
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Implants
    subCategory: 
  - title: Map Generation
    bodyText: The map is randomly generated. You choose your own path to power up
      and eventually reach the boss therefore reaching the new layers.
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Map
    subCategory: Navigation
  - title: Different Layers
    bodyText: For now there is only one layer in game. Rest is W.I.P.
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Map
    subCategory: Navigation
  - title: Combat Node
    bodyText: Begins combat against different foes.
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Map
    subCategory: Nodes
  - title: Implant Node
    bodyText: Gives you three implants to choose from.
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Map
    subCategory: Nodes
  - title: Shop Node
    bodyText: You can buy your desired goods.
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Map
    subCategory: Nodes
  - title: Campfire Node
    bodyText: 'You may choose to rest to replenish your health or level up a random
      implant you own. '
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Map
    subCategory: Nodes
  - title: Elite Combat Node
    bodyText: Here are tougher enemies which yield more gold. Harder to survive but
      better prizes.
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Map
    subCategory: Nodes
  - title: Boss Node
    bodyText: The last node of each layer. Get ready for a tough fight.
    illustration: {fileID: 0}
    category: Map
    subCategory: Nodes
